All true but still potentially not enough.  The problem is each time
they
attack sea creatures have some chance of wrapping around you and
pulling you into the water.  Increase MC to 3, decrease AC to negative
many, max out luck, the chances still don't hit zero.

So it becomes a numbers game.  A character like yours will likely
live 99 times out of 100.  But a character like yours still ends up
dying that once in a hundred, and it's an instakill when it happens.
Given how much effort it takes to run a character up to 199 HP and
facing the Castle, the only 1-in-100 type of chance I want to take
is facing something I need to ascend even if I know at some point
I'll make a dumb mistake and have a YASD to something that
shouldn't have killed me at all.

This is one of the fun parts of Nethack to me.  I can have a buff
character and still end up getting killed.  BUT, being on the
newsgroup I can see it happen to others and potentially avoid
that mistake myself.  Nethack has so many challenges of this
nature that folks play it for years without getting bored.  Progress
slowly in skill and gradually be able for 1 character in many to
survive deeper than ever before, and at some point ascend.



